</ol>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Inorganic_Chemistry/Supplemental_Modules_and_Websites_(Inorganic_Chemistry)/Descriptive_Chemistry/Elements_Organized_by_Block/2_p-Block_Elements/Group_14:_The_Carbon_Family/Z014_Chemistry_of_Silicon_(Z14)" class="mt-section" id="section_25"><span id="Problems"></span><h3 class="lt-chem-559" id="Problems-559">Problems</h3>

<p class="lt-chem-559"><span class="mt-color-ff0000">Highlight area next to &quot;Ans&quot; to see answer</span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">How many oxides does silicon have, and what are they?</p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Ans: <span class="mt-color-ffffff">1 oxide </span><span class="mt-color-ffffff">O<sub>2 </sub></span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559"><span class="mt-color-ffffff"><span class="mt-color-000000">How does a silicate tetra</span></span><span class="mt-color-ffffff"><span class="mt-color-000000">hedral balance its charge if not bonded with another silicate?</span></span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Ans: <span class="mt-color-ffffff">By bondin</span><span class="mt-color-ffffff">g to positively charged metals.</span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Carbon is to organic compounds as silica is to:</p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Ans: <span class="mt-color-ffffff">minerals</span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">How big is the largest silicon-hydrogen compound?</p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Ans: <span class="mt-color-ffffff">The largest silane is hexasilane, with six silicon atoms and fourteen hydrogens.</span></p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Why is silicon important to computers?</p>

<p class="lt-chem-559">Ans: <span class="mt-color-ffffff">It is used to make semiconductors. </span></p>

</div></div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Inorganic_Chemistry/Supplemental_Modules_and_Websites_(Inorganic_Chemistry)/Descriptive_Chemistry/Elements_Organized_by_Block/2_p-Block_Elements/Group_14:_The_Carbon_Family/Z014_Chemistry_of_Silicon_(Z14)" class="mt-section" id="section_26"><span id="Contributors_and_Attributions"></span><h2 class="lt-chem-559" id="Contributors_and_Attributions-559">Contributors and Attributions</h2>

